  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance across equalities programming for ODA eligible countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This component covers all work carried out by Plan International under the PEP-R programme. This includes: 
A Gateway: This serves as a portal for access to key FCDO resources and research on gender and equalities and to showcase and promote evidence and expertise as a global public good.

Funding for the SightSavers Secondee: The secondee will support the Promoting Equalities Programme, to deliver strategic capability building initiatives and senior advisory support across the FCDO&#x2019;s policy teams. The secondee will be responsible for a specific set of objectives and deliverables, agreed in partnership with the Gender and Equalities Department and Sightsavers. They will provide high quality advice and technical support to teams across the FCDO.

The Core Programme Partner Team Costs:
This includes the core operating costs for our consortium of programme partners. This team provides oversight of the programme, expert technical assistance, quality assurance, and advisory support on MEL and safeguarding. Outputs include the development of new cross-cutting guidance, design and delivery of the enabling fund, and training sessions. The consortiums indirect costs / overheads are also included here.</narrative>
  </description>
